<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Poyang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Poyang Lake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Poyang is the largest freshwater lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> province, fed by the Gan and other rivers and draining into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>. Its area varies greatly between the summer flood season and the dry winter months. In 1363 it was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-poyang">Battle of Lake Poyang</a>, in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a>, the future Hongwu Emperor, destroyed the fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a> of Chen Han.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-poyang.jpg" alt="Lake Poyang" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Satelites_image_of_Lake_Poyang.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
